Package: invTwilightFree
Type: Package
Title: Reconstruct Animal Tracks from GLS Tag Data
Version: 0.1.1
Authors@R: c(
    person("Aidan", "Bindoff", email = "aidan.bindoff@utas.edu.au",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Simon", "Wotherspoon", role = "aut"))
Description: Reconstructs animal tracks from continuous light records recorded
    by archival geolocator (GLS) tags. Uses a Sequential Monte Carlo particle
    filter with a spike-and-slab likelihood that directly models the full light
    curve rather than discrete twilight events, making it robust to substantial
    shading noise and sensor anomalies. An optional grid-based hidden Markov
    model supports auxiliary sensor fusion (bathymetry, sea surface temperature,
    spatial priors) via an additive log-likelihood framework. Core computations
    are implemented in Rust for speed.
